# q12-hyperspace-armed.script — Q12 fixture: SPACE with the gate ARMED
#
# D16 row exercised (see test/harness/d16-state-machine.md):
#   - KeyDown ' ' while hyper.hyperspacing is ON: the keypress is IGNORED
#     (no second RemoveShip/NewHyper, no extra RNG draws). Only 'q'/'n'/'h'
#     pass through the armed gate.
#
# Encoding: the first space arms the gate (hyperspacing until random
# re-entry); the second space lands one boundary later — inside the
# hyperspacing window with high probability. The CHECK is backend parity:
# whatever the seeded landing, X11 and GL/VK must observe identical state.
# A repeat-delivery regression (GLFW_REPEAT not dropped) would double-fire
# NewThrust-style RNG consumption here and diverge the trajectories.
#
# Run:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/q12-hyperspace-armed.script \
#       --out DIR --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data

1    capture q12_help

3    keydown s
6    keyup s
40   capture q12_start

50   keydown space             # arms the gate (ship enters hyperspace)
54   keyup space
58   keydown space             # gated: ignored while hyperspacing
62   keyup space
70   capture q12_hyper_single  # exactly ONE teleport in flight
130  capture q12_hyper_back    # one re-entry, seeded position

160  keydown q
164  keyup q
